  "evidencia": "Page: Pandosia (Lucania). Sentence: Plutarch describes Pyrrhus as encamping in the plain between Pandosia and Heraclea, with the river Siris (modern Sinni) in front of him; and the celebrated \"Tabulae Heracleenses\" repeatedly refer to the existence of a town of the name in the immediate neighborhood of Heraclea.\nPage: Pyrrhus of Epirus. Sentence: He was king of the Greek tribe of Molossians, of the royal Aeacid house (from c. 297 BC), and later he became king of Epirus (r. 306–302, 297–272 BC).",
